Seems like an easier solution to these polypiling, ring of conflict type
questions would be to make these actions use up your magical power (although
at some greatly reduced rate, relative to casting spells).  Rings already
use up food points, so adding power shouldn't be hard.  E.g., depending
on how many and what level of monsters you were affecting with a ring of
conflict on, your power would drain at a certain rate; after so many 
moves your power goes to zero, and the ring is useless until you take it 
off for a while(maybe it should remain useless until you've regained enough
power to affect all the surviving monsters for at least one move).  Similar
things could be done for rings of invisibility, levitation, etc.  Polypiling
could drain power depending on the number of things changing, e.g., every
five items polymorphed uses up one point of power.

